   $q$On a town map drawn on a coordinate plane, each unit is 1 block. The library is at $(-5, -3)$ and the school is at $(-5, 8)$. How many blocks apart are they?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$11$ blocks","is_correct":true},{"text":"$8$ blocks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"measured-only-from-the-x-axis"},{"text":"$0$ blocks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-the-x-coordinates"},{"text":"$5$ blocks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-absolute-values-across-zero"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$11$ blocks$q$, $q$Both places have $x$-coordinate $-5$, so they are on the same vertical line. The library is $|-3| = 3$ blocks below the $x$-axis and the school is $|8| = 8$ blocks above it. They are on opposite sides, so the distance is $3 + 8 = 11$ blocks. The choice $5$ blocks subtracts $8 - 3$, as if both were on the same side.$q$, 'draft', null)
